        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0791" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg695"/>

                <head>No. 313.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokei,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1879-10-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 6, 1879</date>. (Received
                        November 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 980.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 959, in which I
                    reported the cholera returns in Japan up to the 6th ultimo, I now beg leave to
                    acquaint you that the report of returns of cholera cases throughout the empire
                    up to the 30th ultimo, as published in the Japan Daily Mail, of the 4th instant,
                    are as follows: Whole number of cases from the commencement of the epidemic in
                    April last, 148,038; of which 83,012 proved fatal; showing that the death-rate
                    of those attacked was 56.07 per cent.</p>
                <p>It is a pleasure to be able to say that the plague is staid, and that but few
                    cases are reported in any quarter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
